<title>USA: COMEX granted dual trading exemption by CFTC.</title>
<headline>COMEX granted dual trading exemption by CFTC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission has told New York Mercantile (NYMEX) that it has granted its COMEX division an exemption for the purposes of dual trading, NYMEX said in a statement.</p>
<p>The exemption allows traders to trade for both themselves and customers in the same market on the same day.</p>
<p>&quot;The Exchange has worked hard, along with the members of both its divisions, to create a self-regulatory structure that offers our customers the fairest and safest possible trading environment,&quot; Exchange President Patrick Thompson said.</p>
<p>NYMEX's COMEX division trades copper, silver and gold.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
